  "name": "ChatView",
  "pinned": false,
  "description": "The conversation addresses a layout issue in the `ChatView.vue` component where the chat name was not occupying the full available width. The solution restructures the header into clear, distinct rows using Tailwind CSS classes. **Row 1** contains the Kanban board breadcrumb and all action buttons (search, toggles, mode switcher, options menu), with a `grow` spacer pushing buttons to the right. **Row 2** places the project/user selectors on the left as `shrink-0` and the chat name in a `flex-1 min-w-0` container that fills all remaining width, using `truncate block min-w-0` on the name `<span>` to enable proper ellipsis truncation for long names. Additional rows handle tags and image strips, keeping the layout clean and scannable.",
